      "side": 1,
      "message": "__va_function() is needed whenever kvm_ksym_ref_nvhe() is used in code that has CFI enabled and the pointer is passed to EL2. In earlier kernel versions, kvm_call_hyp() used to call __kvm_call_hyp(kvm_ksym_ref(f), ...), which went horribly wrong when the compiler replaced the function pointer with a pointer to the jump table (see b/163385976), but it looks like we are not passing function pointers to EL2 anymore. In fact, I don\u0027t see any users of kvm_ksym_ref_nvhe(), so I\u0027ll just drop the __va_function() addition from the other CL. Thanks for pointing this out.",
      "parentUuid": "26d17e18_e0277c92",
